{title: Doxology}
{subtitle: Praise God, from Whom All Blessings Flow}
{lyricist: Thomas Ken}
{composer: Louis Bourgeois}
{year: 1695}
{meta: tune-year 1551}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune OLD HUNDREDTH}
{meta: meter LM (8.8.8.8)}
{meta: variation The doxology, sung to OLD HUNDREDTH}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags praise, Trinity, offering}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Praise God, from [D]whom all [Em]blessings [D]flow;
[G]Praise Him, all [C]creatures [D]here be[G]low;
[G]Praise Him a[D]bove, ye [Em]heavenly [D]host;
[G]Praise Father, [C]Son, and [D]Holy [G]Ghost.
[C]A[G]men.
{end_of_verse}
